-- RPG Excellence | Existing Internal Audit question-bank mapping repair.
-- File 18, corrected: self-contained atomic repair, no temporary tables. Repository location:
-- supabase/migrations/20261028_all_standards_reviewed_coverage_links.sql
-- Paste the COMPLETE file into a NEW Supabase SQL query and run all of it.
-- The DO block is one atomic PostgreSQL statement. Safe to rerun, including
-- after a partially executed older File 18. No temporary-table lifetime is used.
-- Prerequisite: Files 13 (corrected), 15, 16 and 17 already installed.
--
-- Only existing scope-link rows are added. No question is copied, rewritten,
-- retired or deleted. No audit/answer/finding/evidence/approval/user/role/RLS
-- record is changed. The two same-edition laboratory catalogues reuse existing
-- LAB17 question IDs; their existing generic questions and answers remain.
-- The 82 detailed 17024 questions are linked using identical controlled text.
-- EMS/QMS associations below were reviewed against the supplied question text;
-- this is NOT an automatic parent-to-all-descendants clause expansion.
-- Stored content is not a claim of exhaustive published-standard coverage.
--
-- Includes verified repairs for EMS, OH&S, QMS (both catalogue editions),
-- personnel certification and the second laboratory catalogue. The parser and
-- edition-loader files already address the shared problems for the other banks.
-- AS9100 and ISO 19011 lack a matching Assessment inventory in the supplied
-- diagnostic. This migration deliberately leaves those blockers visible.
-- It does not reactivate retired 14001/22301 questions or invent missing banks.
-- Completion still requires live Fieldwork coverage and lead-auditor review.
-- Adding previously missing scope links may expose more unanswered questions.
--
DO $rpg_coverage_repair$
